---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const faq = [
  {
    q: 'What are the three ways to split?',
    a: 'Pull one range out as a single PDF (pages 5 to 8, say, when a portal wants only the signed part); take every page as its own one-page PDF, each with its own download; or cut the file into parts that each fit under a size you set, for portals and mailboxes with a per-file limit.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How does split by size decide the parts?',
    a: 'It measures every page, packs pages in order until the next one would cross your limit, then builds each part and checks its real bytes. A part that still comes out over the limit hands its last page to the next part and is rebuilt. If a single page alone is bigger than the limit, it forms its own part and the result says so.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does splitting change the pages?',
    a: 'No. Pages are copied as they are, not re-drawn or recompressed. A page that goes in as text comes out as text.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How fast is it?',
    a: 'On our bench a 10-page file split in about 21 milliseconds of engine time. The job is effectively instant; picking the range takes longer than the cut.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Where does my PDF go?',
    a: 'Nowhere. It is read into this page and cut in your browser. Watch the network panel while it works if you want to check.',
  },
];
const faqJson = JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faq.map((f) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: f.q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a } })),
});
// HowTo (milestone 5): the steps are this page's own workflow, transcribed
// from its intro, ticket labels and "How it works" text above.
const howToJson = JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'HowTo',
  name: "How to split a PDF by pages or by size",
  step: [
    { '@type': 'HowToStep', position: 1, name: "Pick the PDF", text: "Drop a PDF on the tray, or click to pick one. It stays on this device." },
    { '@type': 'HowToStep', position: 2, name: "Choose the cut", text: "Pick one range as a single PDF (from page, to page), every page as its own PDF, or parts under a size you set in KB." },
    { '@type': 'HowToStep', position: 3, name: "Cut the PDF", text: "Press 'Cut the PDF'. The page opens your PDF, copies the pages you asked for into new files, and saves them. For split by size, each part is built and checked against your limit before it is offered." },
    { '@type': 'HowToStep', position: 4, name: "Download the cut", text: "Download the range as one PDF, each page as its own PDF, or the parts one by one or packed as a single ZIP." },
  ],
});
---

<Base title="Split PDF by pages or by size, free, in your browser · Benchzy" description="Pull a page range out of a PDF as its own file, take every page separately, or cut the file into parts under a size you set. The work runs inside your browser. No upload, no account.">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4">
    <section class="mt-8">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-accent-deep">Job ticket · PDF bench</p>
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl font-black mt-2">Split PDF</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-lg leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
        The pack arrived as one file and the portal wants one part of it, or parts under its
        size limit. Pick the PDF, choose the cut, and take it away. Everything runs in your
        browser; the file is never uploaded. The same range cut from many files at once is on
        the <a class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-accent-deep" href="/batch-split-pdf/">Batch split PDF page</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="ticket mt-6 p-5 sm:p-7" id="sp-tool">
      <div id="sp-tray" class="tray p-6 text-center cursor-pointer" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Pick a PDF">
        <p class="font-display text-xl font-bold">Drop a PDF on the tray, or click to pick one</p>
        <p class="font-mono text-xs text-ink-soft mt-2">PDF · it stays on this device</p>
        <input id="sp-file" type="file" accept="application/pdf,.pdf" class="hidden" />
      </div>

      <div class="grid gap-6 mt-6 md:grid-cols-[1fr_320px]">
        <div>
          <h2 class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft">The cut</h2>
          <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3">
            <label class="flex items-baseline gap-2">
              <input type="radio" name="sp-mode" value="range" checked />
              <span>One range as a single PDF</span>
            </label>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 ml-6 flex-wrap">
              <label class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft" for="sp-from">From page</label>
              <input id="sp-from" type="number" min="1" step="1" value="1" class="border border-ink bg-ticket px-3 py-2 font-mono w-24" />
              <label class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft" for="sp-to">To page</label>
              <input id="sp-to" type="number" min="1" step="1" value="1" class="border border-ink bg-ticket px-3 py-2 font-mono w-24" />
            </div>
            <label class="flex items-baseline gap-2">
              <input type="radio" name="sp-mode" value="each" />
              <span>Every page as its own PDF</span>
            </label>
            <label class="flex items-baseline gap-2">
              <input type="radio" name="sp-mode" value="size" />
              <span>Parts under a size</span>
            </label>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 ml-6 flex-wrap">
              <label class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft" for="sp-size-kb">Each part under (KB)</label>
              <input id="sp-size-kb" type="number" min="50" max="500000" step="50" value="5000" class="border border-ink bg-ticket px-3 py-2 font-mono w-28" />
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2 class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft">File spec</h2>
          <dl id="sp-spec" class="mt-2">
            <div class="spec-row"><dt>file</dt><dd>none picked yet</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <button id="sp-run" class="btn-primary w-full mt-5" type="button" disabled>Cut the PDF</button>
          <p id="sp-status" class="font-mono text-sm mt-4 leading-relaxed" aria-live="polite">Pick a PDF to begin.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div id="sp-result" class="hidden mt-8">
        <div class="tear pt-5 flex items-center gap-4 flex-wrap">
          <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold">Result</h2>
          <span class="stamp" id="sp-stamp">Done on your device</span>
        </div>
        <div id="sp-links" class="mt-4 grid gap-2"></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold border-b-2 border-ink pb-2">How it works</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          The page opens your PDF, copies the pages you asked for into a new file, and saves it.
          Nothing is re-drawn, so the cut is exact and the engine time is measured in milliseconds.
          Splitting is also the smaller-job path for the other benches: a big file that strains a
          phone can be cut here first, then worked on in parts.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold border-b-2 border-ink pb-2">Honest limits</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Taking every page separately gives you one download per page, listed in order; on a long
          document that is a lot of clicks, and split by size packs its parts into a single ZIP
          for the same reason. Split by size deals whole pages, never half a page: a single page
          heavier than your limit forms its own part over the line, and its download line says
          so. A file this page cannot read as a PDF is refused in plain words before any cutting
          happens.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 mb-4">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold border-b-2 border-ink pb-2">Questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-4 grid gap-4">
        {faq.map((f) => (
          <article class="ticket-soft p-5">
            <h3 class="font-bold">{f.q}</h3>
            <p class="text-ink-soft leading-relaxed mt-1">{f.a}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={faqJson}></script>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={howToJson}></script>
  <script>
    import '../scripts/split-pdf.js';
  </script>
</Base>
